1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,999
Clinic AI Agent. WhatsApp and Messenger appointment automation, built with n8n, OpenRouter, Google Calendar and Google Sheets.

2
00:00:03,999 --> 00:00:08,999
Overview. Two production n8n workflows: the Clinic AI Agent (top) and the Booking sub-workflow it calls as tools (bottom).

3
00:00:08,999 --> 00:00:14,999
Step 1 · Message in. A patient messages on WhatsApp or Messenger. Webhooks verify with Meta, acknowledge instantly, and parse each channel's payload.

4
00:00:14,999 --> 00:00:21,000
Step 2 · AI agent. One normalized message reaches the Clinic AI Agent: OpenRouter LLM, conversation memory, and six booking tools.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Step 3 · Tool engine. Every tool calls one sub-workflow. Route by Action branches to clinic info, availability, book, cancel, my bookings, or reschedule.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Step 4 · Real availability. Booking checks live availability first: clinic hours from Google Sheets plus Google Calendar FreeBusy, so a taken slot is never offered.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Step 5 · Book safely. Slot still free? Create the Google Calendar event and append the booking row to Google Sheets. Taken? The patient gets the nearest alternatives.

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Step 6 · Cancel & reschedule. Cancel and reschedule take the same safe path: find the patient's own booking, validate, then update Calendar and Sheets together.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,999
Step 7 · Instant confirmation. The reply is extracted and routed back on the same channel the patient used: Messenger or WhatsApp. Done in seconds, 24/7.

10
00:00:50,999 --> 00:00:55,999
Book, reschedule, cancel, check availability and my bookings. Full case study and workflow files on GitHub.
